projects/new-project-from-range.mdx:9:New Project from Range opens a new project holding exactly the timeline's In–Out range, moved to start at 0. Use it to lift a section out of a long edit to work on by itself. The project you made it from doesn't change. If you only want a file of that section, [export the range](/export/range/) instead.
projects/new-project-from-range.mdx:79:`new_project_from_range` takes the range as times on the top-level timeline, so it doesn't need the In–Out range set, and it won't run while a nest is open. It can also save the new project at a path first, adding `.framejob` if the path lacks it, as long as nothing exists there and no other open project holds it. The assistant asks you before it does that. It returns the new project and how much came along with it. See [Tools: projects and history](/mcp/tools-projects/).
